{"business": {"ko": "퓨런티어는 2009년 설립된 카메라 모듈 관련 자동화장비 전문 기업으로, 2022년 코스닥시장에 상장했다. 사업은 두 부문으로 나뉜다. 장비사업부는 자동차 전장용 카메라 조립 및 검사장비를 개발·판매하고, 부품사업부는 산업용 PC와 LED 광원 등 자동화 장비의 핵심 부품을 만든다. 매출 구성은 집계처마다 차이가 있다. 잡코리아 기업정보(2026년 3월 기준)는 산업용 PC·LED 광원 등 부품 56%, 전장용 장비 32%, 기타 장비 11%로 나눠 보여 준다. 알파스퀘어는 주요 매출원을 산업용 PC, 검사용 LED 광원, 자동화 컴포넌트로 정리한다. 2023년 초 발간된 기업분석 자료에 따르면 2022년 3분기 누적 매출 중 장비 비중은 55.5%, 부품 비중은 44.5%였다. 2025년 장비 매출이 약했던 배경으로는 전장용 카메라 공정장비 수요 둔화와 주요 고객사의 투자 지연이 외부 분석에서 꼽혔다(에프앤가이드). 부품 쪽은 산업용 자동화와 검사 설비 수요에 기대는 구조다. 신사업으로는 전장용 라이다 및 ToF 모듈 공정 장비 개발을 마친 뒤 초도 매출이 발생했다. 기업모니터는 2026년 1분기에 산업용 PC와 LED 광원 부품, 전장용 카메라 장비의 수주가 늘었다고 전했다. 경쟁 구도는 고객사의 투자 계획과 장비 성능에 따라 좌우되는 구조이다.", "en": "Furonteer is an automation equipment specialist for camera module production, founded in 2009 and listed on KOSDAQ in 2022. The business runs in two divisions. The equipment division develops and sells assembly and inspection tools for automotive camera modules, while the parts division makes core components for automation equipment, including industrial PCs and LED light sources. Revenue mix varies by data provider. Jobkorea company information, as of March 2026, shows parts such as industrial PCs and LED lighting at 56%, automotive equipment at 32%, and other equipment at 11%. Alphasquare lists its main revenue sources as industrial PCs, inspection LED light sources, and automation components. A research report published in early 2023 showed equipment at 55.5% and parts at 44.5% of cumulative revenue for the first nine months of 2022. External analysis (FnGuide) cited weaker demand for automotive camera process equipment and investment delays by major customers as reasons for the 2025 equipment slowdown. The parts side depends on demand from industrial automation and inspection facilities. In new products, Furonteer completed development of process equipment for automotive lidar and ToF modules and then recorded first sales. According to Wisereport, orders for industrial PC and LED light parts and automotive camera equipment increased in the first quarter of 2026. Competitive positioning depends on customer investment plans and equipment performance."}}
===JSON_END===

280360-37992b58c7bee44a7fe6317d.text:
===JSON_START===
{"0": "In Q3 2026, overseas subsidiaries' operating profit rose 137.8% to KRW 23.1 billion, and cumulative overseas operating profit for Q1–Q3 increased 105.4% to KRW 64.7 billion. India sales grew 22.6% to KRW 90.5 billion in Q3, and media reports say Choco Pie's market share there exceeds 70%. The company set a target of KRW 1 trillion in sales for its India subsidiary by 2032. If overseas growth continues, it could become a pillar supporting consolidated operating profit.", "1": "Operating profit rose for two consecutive quarters in 2026, from KRW 35.8 billion in Q1 to KRW 64.7 billion in Q2 and KRW 89.9 billion in Q3. The Q3 operating margin was 7.7%, up from 6.0% a year earlier (preliminary). Net income attributable to controlling shareholders also rose from KRW 17.3 billion in Q1 to KRW 50.8 billion in Q3, bringing the sum of the last four quarters to KRW 87.7 billion. The fact that profitability has continued for a third straight quarter since the loss-making Q4 2025 is the basis for the bullish view.", "2": "In the domestic business, Q3 sales fell 1.7% to KRW 918.2 billion, but operating profit rose 10.3% to KRW 69.4 billion. The company is cutting its cost structure by shutting down the Natuur store business and cleaning up low-efficiency products and sales channels. Production network optimization and logistics and procurement innovation were presented as tasks for improving profitability. It is also a positive that dry confectionery sales grew 4.6%, giving the domestic business a relatively strong segment.", "3": "Domestic sales fell 1.7% to KRW 918.2 billion in Q3 2026, and ice cream sales declined 7.4% to KRW 225.3 billion. Reports cited a shrinking domestic ice cream market and the cleanup of low-efficiency products as the background. Ending the Natuur store business reduces the cost burden but is also a factor shrinking the top line. If domestic sales keep falling, overseas subsidiaries will account for an even larger share of consolidated profit.", "4": "Operating profit declined from a peak of KRW 177.0 billion in 2023 to KRW 109.5 billion in 2025, and the company posted an operating loss of KRW 10.5 billion in Q4 2025. Net income attributable to controlling shareholders also swung to a net loss of KRW 17.8 billion in the same quarter. Profits have continued since Q1 2026, but the recovery period is only three quarters. How long the profitable trend lasts needs to be confirmed in the quarterly figures of the next periodic report.", "5": "Reports pointed to international uncertainty from the Middle East war and the burden of key raw materials as headwinds for the earnings environment. The debt-to-equity ratio rose from 94.4% in 2022 to 100.0% in 2025. Operating cash flow fell from KRW 453.0 billion in 2023 to KRW 231.1 billion in 2025. If increases in raw material costs are not sufficiently reflected in selling prices, margin pressure could continue.", "6": "According to reports, higher oil prices and raw material price volatility caused by the Middle East war were mentioned as cost burdens. Overseas subsidiaries are affected not only by raw materials but also by local logistics and exchange rates. Since the operating margin fell as low as 2.6% in 2025, profit could react sensitively to cost changes. The speed at which higher costs are passed through to selling prices is the key variable.", "7": "Overseas subsidiaries' operating profit in Q3 was reported to be about one-quarter of total operating profit. Growth is concentrated in a single product, Choco Pie in India, and in two regions, India and Kazakhstan. If local competition intensifies or demand slows, profit volatility could increase. As India production capacity is being expanded, managing the utilization rate is also a task.", "8": "At the end of 2025, total liabilities were KRW 2,287.3 billion, almost the same size as total equity of KRW 2,286.7 billion. The debt-to-equity ratio rose from 94.4% in 2022 to 100.0% in 2025. Operating cash flow fell from KRW 453.0 billion in 2023 to KRW 231.1 billion in 2025. Along with whether the profit recovery lasts, cash generation capacity and debt management should be watched together."}
===JSON_END===

